{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791235694,"nonce":"Fq0bY7p267nvCURLjLE4I846eQo=","message":"Upgrade to taffy 0.14 is done locally on branch taffy-0.14 (47d2a670, f0deb31c), not pushed. The avatar-row test passes on 0.14 and is no longer ignored.\n\nWhat it took in Blinc:\n- Length types are compact values: constructors became Dimension::length/percent/auto, and matches go through expand(). about 370 constructor lines, 32 min_size/max_size sites (those fields are now Size\u003cLengthPercentageAuto\u003e).\n- AlignItems, AlignContent and their aliases are structs with constants (CENTER, FLEX_START, ...), not enums.\n- The text measure function now returns a LayoutOutput; it wraps the old body in compute_leaf_layout.\n- Layout.content_size is gone; get_content_size reads scrollable_overflow_rect right/bottom.\n- taffy::Style is neither Send nor Sync, because CompactLength is a tagged *const (). Only StatefulInner kept one across threads, so it holds a SharedStyle wrapper with an unsafe impl Send/Sync. It is sound while no calc() length is ever stored; Blinc builds none, but nothing enforces that for a downstream crate.\n- diff.rs hashed alignment values with mem::discriminant. On a struct that is unspecified, so style diffing would have ignored alignment changes. Now hashed through keyword() and is_safe().\n\nChecked against 0.6 on the same scenes: layout rects for 8 flex/margin/absolute/text scenes identical (51 nodes), content sizes for 12 scroll-container scenes identical, baseline_capture pixel-identical, full nextest 1527 passed, wasm32 checks and clippy clean, MSRV unaffected (taffy 0.14 needs 1.71).\n\nNot done: blinc_node_editor pins taffy 0.6 and builds styles for Blinc's tree, so the examples node-editor feature does not compile until it moves. Migrated in a scratch clone (one file, 60 lines; its 80 unit tests pass against this Blinc) but not pushed. Order: push node_editor, bump its pin in examples/blinc_app_examples/Cargo.toml, then push Blinc, or --all-features CI is red in between.","files":null}]}